1
00:00:00,833 --> 00:00:05,033
FluxFlow reconstructs a higher resolution
astronomical image from a ground

2
00:00:05,033 --> 00:00:08,933
based observation. The goal is to recover
structure and source brightness,

3
00:00:09,133 --> 00:00:11,733
while avoiding objects the measurement does not
support.

4
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:17,800
DESI provides the blurred, noisy ground based
input.

5
00:00:18,067 --> 00:00:21,600
The Hubble Space Telescope supplies a sharper
observational reference.

6
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:25,467
FluxFlow estimates a two times or four times
reconstruction;

7
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,000
it does not replace a new Hubble observation.

8
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:34,733
The DESI Hubble dataset uses aligned
observations, not synthetic blur

9
00:00:34,733 --> 00:00:38,467
alone. The paper studies about 19,500 pairs.

10
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:46,033
The prepared version contains 19,438 pairs per
scale, together with reliability maps and source
labels.

11
00:00:48,367 --> 00:00:50,767
Regression models can oversmooth fine detail.

12
00:00:51,033 --> 00:00:55,033
Generative models can turn noise into plausible
stars or galaxies.

13
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:59,167
These hallucinated sources can bias catalogues
and flux measurements.

14
00:00:59,433 --> 00:01:01,800
Looking sharper is not enough for scientific
use.

15
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,433
FluxFlow learns a continuous flow from Gaussian
noise to a reconstructed

16
00:01:08,433 --> 00:01:11,000
image, conditioned on the DESI observation.

17
00:01:11,267 --> 00:01:15,700
It works directly in pixel space, avoiding a
lossy latent image compressor.

18
00:01:18,367 --> 00:01:19,900
Training combines two weights.

19
00:01:20,167 --> 00:01:24,333
Hubble inverse variance maps reduce the
influence of unreliable pixels.

20
00:01:24,633 --> 00:01:27,967
Source region masks give stars and galaxies
greater importance.

21
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:31,867
These reference derived maps supervise training,
not inference.

22
00:01:34,467 --> 00:01:38,267
During sampling, blur and downsample the
candidate reconstruction with

23
00:01:38,267 --> 00:01:42,167
a physical forward model. Compare that
projection with the observed DESI

24
00:01:42,167 --> 00:01:47,000
image. The difference is a residual that reveals
inconsistency with the measurement.

25
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:54,467
A Wiener regularized back projection turns that
residual into a high resolution

26
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:58,600
correction. Repeating the check at every flow
step suppresses unsupported

27
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:02,800
structure. The regularization helps avoid
cumulative blur from repeated

28
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,300
ordinary back projections.

29
00:02:06,667 --> 00:02:10,100
The paper compares FluxFlow with regression and
generative baselines at

30
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:14,600
both scales. Inspect the same stars and galaxies
against the Hubble reference,

31
00:02:14,833 --> 00:02:18,300
rather than treating a visually convincing
texture as evidence.

32
00:02:21,333 --> 00:02:24,933
FluxFlow achieves the lowest source flux error
among the compared methods:

33
00:02:25,133 --> 00:02:30,233
2.959 at two times and 3.755 at four times.

34
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:38,133
Structural similarity reaches 0.714 and 0.570,
respectively, with the latter tied for best.

35
00:02:41,033 --> 00:02:42,767
Ablations explain the mechanism.

36
00:02:43,033 --> 00:02:46,067
Without measurement consistency, false sources
increase.

37
00:02:46,367 --> 00:02:49,767
Without Wiener correction, repeated projections
broaden sources.

38
00:02:50,067 --> 00:02:53,867
Reliability weighting also reduces learning from
instrumental defects.

39
00:02:54,133 --> 00:02:56,800
Each component serves a different scientific
purpose.

40
00:02:59,333 --> 00:03:01,833
Hallucinations are reduced, not eliminated.

41
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:06,267
The historical patch split contains overlapping
sky regions, so its reported

42
00:03:06,267 --> 00:03:10,233
results should not be read as spatially
independent generalization.

43
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:13,333
More demanding scientific validation remains
necessary.

44
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:20,733
Future research includes explicit joint
denoising, multispectral reconstruction,

45
00:03:20,867 --> 00:03:22,667
and uncertainty calibrated sampling.

46
00:03:22,967 --> 00:03:26,167
Broader telescope and noise conditions need
further evaluation.

47
00:03:26,433 --> 00:03:31,133
These are research directions, not capabilities
demonstrated by the current single band system.

48
00:03:33,733 --> 00:03:37,800
Explore the paper and code to understand how
FluxFlow balances restored

49
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,933
detail with observational evidence.

50
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:44,367
Conservative reconstruction is a step toward
more reliable astronomical imaging.

